WEBVTT

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:16.850
<i>That's why...</i>

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:19.430
<i>I made their wish come true.</i>

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:37.700
<i>If everything is an illusion...</i>

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:42.330
<i>If everything is destiny...</i>

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:45.500
<i>A song that awakens and calls...</i>

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:48.710
<i>The sound of a budding wish...</i>

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:54.970
<i>What we light up in the sky...</i>

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:57.840
<i>from which light has disappeared...</i>

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:37.930
THE SONG OF HEALING

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:51.650
Hey, Mel. I wonder if the Capital
is farther away than the stars.

00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:54.280
I wonder.

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:58.110
If that were the case,
we'd get hungry before we got there.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:00.030
You're always thinking about eating.

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:04.540
I guess it doesn't matter.
I can't go anyway.

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:07.750
You aren't going, Rin?

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:10.630
Then I'll go on my own first.

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:12.130
What are you saying, Al?

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:14.550
How come you get to go to the Capital?

00:02:15.550 --> 00:02:17.880
Now that I've completed this invention,

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:21.470
there's no way the engineers
in the Capital can ignore me.

00:02:21.550 --> 00:02:23.100
There he goes again.

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:24.970
What did you make this time?

00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:27.430
This is my newest invention.

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:29.440
An automatic peeler!

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:32.060
What?! Does it work?

00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:34.860
Of course! Take a close look!

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:44.410
What do you think?!
It's a genius invention!

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:48.410
What a waste.

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:50.710
Too bad.

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:53.880
That's impossible.
I considered the apple's mass

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:57.380
-and the friction resistance of the blade.
-If that's your best work,

00:02:57.460 --> 00:02:59.300
you're never going to the Capital.

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:02.510
-I fixed it so many times.
-You don't need to go to the Capital.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:05.930
Grandpa.

00:03:08.770 --> 00:03:10.310
I've told you before.

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:13.230
It's not a place for countryfolk like us.

00:03:13.690 --> 00:03:15.900
That's exactly why I want to go!

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:20.200
The Capital is filled with lots of people.
And they're all so fashionable!

00:03:20.570 --> 00:03:22.950
I'd love to be able to sing there.

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:23.870
No.

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:29.330
Also, I heard the Capital has
a Court Orchestra!

00:03:29.410 --> 00:03:32.080
I'm gonna sing with their gorgeous music--

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:33.290
That's not happening!

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:36.460
Grandpa...

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:39.460
I thought I forbade you from singing.

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:42.430
Especially that song.

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:45.350
You must never sing it.

00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:54.810
I'm definitely going to sing
at the Capital someday!

00:03:59.990 --> 00:04:02.320
Everyone, the song is going to start!

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:04.990
Miss Finis is going to sing!

00:04:05.070 --> 00:04:06.200
Miss Finis?!

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:09.450
She's at the palace!
The song is going to start!

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:23.590
<i>O AQUA</i>
<i>From a sacred prayer</i>

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:28.680
<i>O AQUA</i>

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:32.390
<i>To a connection with life</i>

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:35.100
I wonder why Grandpa hates singing.

00:04:35.190 --> 00:04:36.100
Isn't it obvious?

00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:37.110
<i>I wish to receive</i>

00:04:37.190 --> 00:04:38.520
-What?
-When you sing, Rin,

00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:40.820
things that are
scientifically impossible happen!

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:43.450
<i>We ask for your blessings</i>

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:45.030
<i>I like your songs, Rin.</i>

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:49.910
You know, a power that only gets activated

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:51.500
<i>And offer everything now</i>

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:54.750
when you use certain scales and lyrics,
that's just weird!

00:04:57.460 --> 00:04:58.960
<i>It flows</i>

00:04:59.380 --> 00:05:02.510
<i>O AQUA</i>

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:06.090
<i>When filled</i>

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:08.600
<i>With pure blue</i>

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:09.810
<i>I can't believe this.</i>

00:05:09.890 --> 00:05:13.350
It's not about some ancient magic
they believed in ages ago.

00:05:13.430 --> 00:05:14.940
<i>We will play...</i>

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:16.520
Magic, huh?

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:24.820
<i>A melody of gratitude</i>

00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:31.700
Oh, Miss Finis!

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:33.370
-Miss Finis!
-Miss Finis!

00:05:33.450 --> 00:05:35.120
She created water with her song!

00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:36.920
She's a god! A goddess!

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:39.000
Now we will prosper!

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:51.720
Miss Finis, over here.

00:05:52.470 --> 00:05:55.730
-Corte.
-You really are bad with directions.

00:05:55.810 --> 00:05:58.020
Well, don't the roads look alike?

00:05:58.100 --> 00:05:58.980
They do not.

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:03.190
Come. It's time to watch
the swordsmanship competition.

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:04.230
Yes.

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:07.200
She's a bit of an airhead,
but that makes her cute.

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:09.280
I hear she's marrying
into the royal family.

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:11.280
She's marrying that prince?

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:14.370
-That's terrible.
-Hey! Watch what you say.

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:29.130
Point! That's it!

00:06:43.900 --> 00:06:44.770
Forgive me.

00:06:46.940 --> 00:06:47.780
Are you hurt?

00:06:49.490 --> 00:06:50.860
The winner is Leobolt.

00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:52.370
Henry Leobolt!

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:57.330
Leobolt, that was splendid.

00:06:57.830 --> 00:06:59.160
Yes, sir, Prince Rudo.

00:06:59.790 --> 00:07:04.790
But next time, don't do anything stupid,
like showing concern for the loser.

00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:07.880
If this were a battlefield, you'd be dead.

00:07:09.470 --> 00:07:10.300
Yes, sir.

00:07:17.890 --> 00:07:19.140
That was splendid...

00:07:20.350 --> 00:07:21.810
knight from the Leobolt family.

00:07:22.900 --> 00:07:23.980
Miss Finis!

00:07:27.150 --> 00:07:31.280
The Leobolt family has excelled
in the martial arts for many generations.

00:07:32.070 --> 00:07:34.450
I don't have any battlefield experience.

00:07:34.870 --> 00:07:37.660
And to tell you the truth,
I hate hurting people.

00:07:37.740 --> 00:07:39.370
Is that so?

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:44.250
-I'm a failure as a knight of the Capital.
-No...

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:48.090
Where are you headed now?

00:07:48.670 --> 00:07:50.920
To visit lords in the countryside.

00:07:51.420 --> 00:07:53.300
Then does that mean...?

00:07:54.090 --> 00:07:56.640
Yes. A war is coming.

00:08:02.980 --> 00:08:06.150
<i>I wish all the fighting... would stop.</i>

00:08:12.150 --> 00:08:13.530
I'm so bored.

00:08:16.410 --> 00:08:17.620
It's so soft.

00:08:27.630 --> 00:08:29.630
-I'm tired of this!
-Hey!

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:33.220
What do you think about going
to the Capital? Just us?

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:36.140
You know...

00:08:37.180 --> 00:08:42.230
The Capital is here. Our village is
way past the edge of this map.

00:08:45.310 --> 00:08:48.020
I wish we had the money
to take a flying ship...

00:08:49.020 --> 00:08:53.070
<i>I've been called by the sky</i>

00:08:53.530 --> 00:08:57.870
<i>My longing has become wings</i>

00:08:58.490 --> 00:09:03.040
<i>That place that I've been dreaming about</i>

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:07.830
<i>Is waiting for me</i>

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:10.130
Rin, can you give me a hand?

00:09:11.420 --> 00:09:13.090
Are Mel and Al there, too?

00:09:14.090 --> 00:09:16.260
You two go gather some nuts.

00:09:18.550 --> 00:09:20.470
I want to go to the forest, too.

00:09:20.810 --> 00:09:22.350
Okay, go ahead.

00:09:22.930 --> 00:09:25.690
-I'll help out here.
-Are you sure?

00:09:26.190 --> 00:09:29.020
In return, make sure
you bring back lots of nuts!

00:09:31.190 --> 00:09:32.230
I love you!

00:09:33.530 --> 00:09:34.360
Hey!

00:09:35.570 --> 00:09:40.080
<i>Please don't stop me</i>

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:44.870
<i>Singing is like wings for my heart</i>

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:49.630
<i>If I spread my wings far</i>

00:09:49.710 --> 00:09:55.090
<i>My wishes will come true someday</i>

00:09:59.550 --> 00:10:01.510
Mel is too nice to you.

00:10:02.060 --> 00:10:06.230
Do you think so?
But Grandpa is so strict.

00:10:06.310 --> 00:10:08.020
Well, I guess that's true...

00:10:08.900 --> 00:10:11.860
-What was that?
-Is--? Is it a wild boar?

00:10:11.940 --> 00:10:13.780
No way. We could have a feast!

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:17.030
Hold on! Wild boars are pretty violent!

00:10:17.110 --> 00:10:18.610
You have to be careful...

00:10:22.410 --> 00:10:23.240
What--?

00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:25.950
He's a knight from the Capital!

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:27.750
Are you okay?

00:10:28.250 --> 00:10:32.040
Medicine isn't my specialty,
but he's clearly in poor condition.

00:10:33.130 --> 00:10:34.590
-What?
-Ice!

00:10:34.960 --> 00:10:37.010
How does this kind of phenomenon happen?

00:10:37.090 --> 00:10:38.420
That doesn't matter!

00:10:38.930 --> 00:10:40.800
He's in pain.

00:10:41.590 --> 00:10:45.560
Medicine! Let's go to the village
and bring back some medicine.

00:10:46.930 --> 00:10:49.440
-Rin!
-We don't have enough time.

00:10:51.020 --> 00:10:51.940
That song...

00:10:52.860 --> 00:10:54.650
I'm going to sing that song.

00:10:55.020 --> 00:10:58.030
You can't! Grandpa said you mustn't--

00:10:58.110 --> 00:10:59.400
Even so, I--

00:11:01.110 --> 00:11:02.570
I can't leave him like this.

00:11:10.580 --> 00:11:12.880
<i>A song that</i>

00:11:13.290 --> 00:11:16.050
<i>Awakens and calls</i>

00:11:16.920 --> 00:11:19.670
<i>People repeat the song</i>

00:11:20.170 --> 00:11:22.550
<i>In their hearts</i>

00:11:23.260 --> 00:11:25.810
<i>I wish to shine love</i>

00:11:26.100 --> 00:11:29.060
<i>Into the sky</i>

00:11:29.810 --> 00:11:34.480
<i>From which the light has disappeared</i>

00:11:39.240 --> 00:11:41.950
So this is the Song of Healing...

00:11:43.780 --> 00:11:45.910
It heals all wounds.

00:11:47.160 --> 00:11:48.700
The power of Rin's songs...

00:11:52.420 --> 00:11:53.460
Who are you?

00:11:58.050 --> 00:11:59.510
What a surprise.

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:05.300
Finis!

00:12:06.260 --> 00:12:07.350
Prince Rudo.

00:12:09.350 --> 00:12:13.270
We're going to have a banquet
to lift the morale of the Capital Army.

00:12:13.350 --> 00:12:15.860
We're going to have you sing again.

00:12:18.110 --> 00:12:20.530
I'll get ready to sing
the Song of Healing.

00:12:21.030 --> 00:12:24.740
By the way, that song you sung
the other day was splendid.

00:12:25.070 --> 00:12:26.820
The people loved it.

00:12:26.910 --> 00:12:31.660
Yes. Even if the dry spell continues,
we won't run out of water anymore.

00:12:31.750 --> 00:12:33.330
What are you talking about?

00:12:34.790 --> 00:12:39.420
That waterfall is just a natural barrier
to protect the east side of the palace.

00:12:40.420 --> 00:12:42.590
What about the water supply
for the people?

00:12:42.670 --> 00:12:44.510
Of course we don't have any for them!

00:12:44.590 --> 00:12:48.260
Beggars who don't have enough money
to buy water should leave.

00:12:49.140 --> 00:12:50.220
How can you say that?

00:12:50.850 --> 00:12:53.640
I sang that song for the people...

00:12:56.350 --> 00:13:00.070
Making the Capital stronger is
what's best for the people.

00:13:00.820 --> 00:13:02.650
A war is starting soon.

00:13:03.650 --> 00:13:07.200
All you have to do is use
the power of your songs.

00:13:09.990 --> 00:13:11.370
So, you're Rin and Al?

00:13:12.540 --> 00:13:15.250
My name is Leobolt.
I'm a knight of the Capital.

00:13:15.330 --> 00:13:18.210
You're the first person
from the Capital I've met!

00:13:18.290 --> 00:13:19.790
You saved my life.

00:13:20.290 --> 00:13:22.340
But how did you heal my wounds?

00:13:23.420 --> 00:13:24.510
Um...

00:13:24.840 --> 00:13:27.640
We used the best medicine in the village!

00:13:27.720 --> 00:13:30.220
-You got better right away.
-Yes, yes, yes.

00:13:30.300 --> 00:13:31.640
Is that so?

00:13:32.810 --> 00:13:33.930
I must repay you.

00:13:34.350 --> 00:13:38.150
Did you hear that Al? See!
Good things happen when I sing.

00:13:38.480 --> 00:13:39.860
Well...

00:13:41.610 --> 00:13:45.570
We want to go to the Capital!
You know the Star Song Festival, right?

00:13:45.650 --> 00:13:48.570
It's where your wishes come true
if you sing to the stars.

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:49.950
We want to see it.

00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:53.580
That's scientifically impossible.

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:55.120
Shut up.

00:13:55.830 --> 00:13:58.420
Anyway, please take us to the Capital!

00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:00.500
The Capital, huh?

00:14:07.720 --> 00:14:10.640
This is bad. Staying here is dangerous.
Let's run!

00:14:12.890 --> 00:14:15.350
What in the world is going on?

00:14:18.020 --> 00:14:18.850
Rin?

00:14:20.940 --> 00:14:21.770
I can hear it.

00:14:23.860 --> 00:14:25.030
I can hear a song...

00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:31.120
What is this?

00:14:33.330 --> 00:14:34.240
Run!

00:14:45.050 --> 00:14:45.880
Rin...

00:14:49.050 --> 00:14:50.800
Hey, what was that?

00:14:50.890 --> 00:14:54.850
I don't know!
It's scientifically impossible!

00:14:54.930 --> 00:14:56.600
-Mr. Leobolt!
-That's--

00:15:05.940 --> 00:15:06.900
Mr. Leobolt?

00:15:07.360 --> 00:15:09.320
Rin, Al! Are you okay?

00:15:09.400 --> 00:15:10.410
-Yes.
-Yes.

00:15:10.490 --> 00:15:14.280
You guys run away!
I'm the one those guys are after!

00:15:14.660 --> 00:15:15.990
-Those guys?
-Go!

00:15:17.370 --> 00:15:18.200
Rin.

00:15:24.710 --> 00:15:27.050
Forgive me... Please get away safely.

00:15:35.180 --> 00:15:36.970
Hey, Al. What's going on?

00:15:37.970 --> 00:15:40.560
Why is this happening to us
all of a sudden?

00:15:40.940 --> 00:15:43.400
I don't know. I don't know.

00:15:43.650 --> 00:15:45.730
Is it because I didn't obey Grandpa?

00:15:46.770 --> 00:15:49.650
Is it because I said I wanted to go
to the Capital?

00:15:49.740 --> 00:15:50.740
Who's there?

00:15:59.250 --> 00:16:00.960
They're late...

00:16:01.830 --> 00:16:04.460
It's because you let them go
to the forest alone.

00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:05.960
Sorry.

00:16:06.880 --> 00:16:09.510
She'd better not be singing again.

00:16:10.300 --> 00:16:12.220
I think it's okay for her to sing.

00:16:12.300 --> 00:16:13.220
No.

00:16:13.760 --> 00:16:15.220
It's her dream.

00:16:18.350 --> 00:16:21.390
I love Rin's songs.

00:16:22.600 --> 00:16:24.690
I want her to sing at the Capital.

00:16:25.270 --> 00:16:28.770
I'm sure she'll be able
to cheer up lots of people.

00:16:28.860 --> 00:16:30.650
Rin's songs are dangerous.

00:16:31.490 --> 00:16:33.450
Why do you hate them so much?

00:16:34.160 --> 00:16:35.990
Why are you so hard on Rin?

00:16:36.820 --> 00:16:40.450
Is it because she's not related to you
by blood, like me and Al?

00:16:40.540 --> 00:16:41.870
Don't be silly!

00:16:42.830 --> 00:16:44.960
She's a true member of our family.

00:16:45.880 --> 00:16:47.380
Just like you two.

00:16:47.960 --> 00:16:49.590
You're my grandchildren.

00:16:49.670 --> 00:16:51.510
-Then...
-Mel,

00:16:52.380 --> 00:16:54.800
you'll be the only one to know about this.

00:16:56.300 --> 00:16:57.430
About the power...

00:16:58.720 --> 00:17:00.720
of Rin's songs.

00:17:04.140 --> 00:17:05.600
Who are you?

00:17:11.030 --> 00:17:13.650
It's been a long time, Hawkray!

00:17:16.070 --> 00:17:18.910
Bring out the girl who sings.

00:17:25.120 --> 00:17:26.370
Come out now!

00:17:32.420 --> 00:17:33.760
Hey! That's enough!

00:17:35.420 --> 00:17:38.800
-Come back.
-No. I heard a sound over here.

00:17:39.220 --> 00:17:40.050
What?

00:17:42.140 --> 00:17:43.270
It's just a dog.

00:17:44.350 --> 00:17:47.650
That's enough. Let's go.
The general discovered a village.

00:17:47.980 --> 00:17:49.150
We're going back.

00:17:50.110 --> 00:17:51.900
You could have told me earlier.

00:17:51.980 --> 00:17:54.360
We won't make it in time
for the prince's speech.

00:17:56.650 --> 00:18:00.070
They were talking about a village.
Al, it can't be...

00:18:00.660 --> 00:18:01.490
A village...?

00:18:02.120 --> 00:18:03.160
It can't be...

00:18:04.450 --> 00:18:06.460
War is approaching!

00:18:07.920 --> 00:18:12.420
Enemies who threaten our Capital
have begun their invasion!

00:18:13.550 --> 00:18:17.430
If we lose this war, we lose everything.

00:18:17.880 --> 00:18:19.590
<i>Our people, our homes, our money.</i>

00:18:19.970 --> 00:18:23.510
Even our history will be taken from us!

00:18:30.560 --> 00:18:32.400
<i>That is why we must fight!</i>

00:18:33.150 --> 00:18:36.650
That is why we must draw our swords!

00:18:36.740 --> 00:18:39.110
Yeah!

00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:50.170
<i>This is a war of justice to prevent</i>
<i>the enemy from taking what's ours.</i>

00:18:51.960 --> 00:18:53.500
<i>But do not worry.</i>

00:18:54.300 --> 00:18:57.130
The Goddess of Victory is on our side!

00:18:59.630 --> 00:19:03.260
An absolute goddess who possesses
the power of miracles!

00:19:09.980 --> 00:19:10.850
<i>Rin?</i>

00:19:14.900 --> 00:19:15.730
Mel?

00:19:17.280 --> 00:19:19.110
-Mel!
-Mel!

00:19:31.040 --> 00:19:32.080
I'm so glad...

00:19:33.460 --> 00:19:35.340
you're both safe.

00:19:37.130 --> 00:19:43.050
<i>A song that awakens and calls</i>

00:19:43.430 --> 00:19:48.680
<i>People repeat the song in their hearts</i>

00:19:48.770 --> 00:19:49.930
<i>It's my fault.</i>

00:19:50.020 --> 00:19:51.350
<i>I wish to shine love</i>

